{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies","id":1022594,"title":"On the Spontaneous Arising of Non-Iremite Mummies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-26T19:59:08-08:00","id":1022594,"title":"On the Spontaneous Arising of Non-Iremite Mummies","content":"...Or, What Happens When You Poke Fate With A Stick.<br /> <br /> The Deceived character book presents an Apotheosis scenario of tortured servitude to demented memory-ghosts for an arguably better, but certainly more peaceful, servitude to Fate itself, with said Arisen being called to action when (and in some cases, <i>where)</i> Fate wills.<br /> <br /> My supposition: that with the Shan'iatu/Judges of Duat/whoever creating the Arisen (as in, actually making such a thing <i>possible in the first place</i>), they gouged a hole in the fabric of existence, leaving a void to be filled/a channel to be used. Now further supposing that Fate can, on some level, make decisions (which is somewhat implied by the aforementioned situation with the Deceived), then could it not be possible Fate Itself to decree (ha!) that a given situation is suitable enough that a new Arisen could be created? Furthermore, is it not possible that this new being could, absent any interference save (again) that of Fate Itself, develop abilities with basis, effects, and imagery, unlike anything the Custodians of Irem have ever seen before?<br /> <br /> And if such a thing as all this <b>is</b> possible<b>,</b> then the question becomes &quot;Why <b>would</b> such a thing happen?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I believe that an answer as good as any regarding such an unknowable force as Fate can be summed up as &quot;Because they <b>pissed it <i>off</i></b> .&quot;<br /> <br /> The End Result? Ghost Jaguars raiding museums of mesoamerican antiquities and sudden rains of sakura blossoms rendering cultists too stunned at the perfect beauty of the moment to defend their mistress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T21:02:48-08:00","id":1022607,"title":"","content":"I maintain that the Rite of Return was a singular occult act that required the ritual sacrifice of <i>an entire empire</i> to fuel it at the direct behest of some godlike supernatural entities whose origins we don't truly understand, and that duplicating that is both silly and undermines the fundamental loneliness and temporal distance that the Arisen experience that provides some of the thematic core of the game.<br /> <br /> But I'm no fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T00:15:29-08:00","id":1022640,"title":"","content":"Well, in the first place I don't see Fate being that sentient or self-willed as you describe. It's not a task leader summoning the undead for its top secret cosmic missions.<br /> <br /> In the second place, though, if Fate <i>were</i> more sentient then I don't think it would create new mummies as its agents. Those Deceived that it uses are some of their most valued servants, but I think that's a coincidence...or, given the topic of discussion, a 'circumstance' of fate. All I mean is that they're more like <i>adopted </i>servitors.<br /> <br /> Were I going to introduce beings who were more directed by and in tune with Fate I would look to some horrifying Sam Araya versions of Norns and Moirae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T19:57:53-08:00","id":1023083,"title":"","content":"Worth noting: In canon, there is exactly <i>one</i> Ascended mummy. And he's not a Deceived.<br /> <br /> Fatewalkers are a possibility in the setting, but for now Mummy's Fate just does shit by virtue of being The Way Things Are (And Were Always Going To Be).<br /> <br /> All other notes are true. It's worth noting that mummies are aberrations of nature and a defiance of fate-hell, that's why they can <i>defy fate</i>.*<br /> <br /> *As conceived of in the Curse sense, as opposed to Lost or Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:25:05-08:00","id":1023096,"title":"","content":"I'd say Fate prefers having mundane actors, who may or may not have peculiar abilities regarding Sekhem and Relics, be positioned in just the right time and just the right space so they can screw up the still-loyal servants of the Shan'iatu. Which is kinda similar to how the God-Machine's Infrastructure work.<br /> <br /> Employing Fatewalkers would be something like dispatching Sidereal Exalted to a scene that could have been fixed by a pattern spider tying up some loose knots here and there. (Note: I don't know that much of Exalted lore, so shoot me if the analogy is weird)<br /> <br /> By the way, are &quot;Fatewalkers&quot; an official name for liberated Deceived?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:27:07-08:00","id":1023097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1023096#post1023096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Fate prefers having mundane actors, who may or may not have peculiar abilities regarding Sekhem and Relics, be positioned in just the right time and just the right space so they can screw up the still-loyal servants of the Shan'iatu. Which is kinda similar to how the God-Machine's Infrastructure work.<br /> <br /> Employing Fatewalkers would be something like dispatching Sidereal Exalted to a scene that could have been fixed by a pattern spider tying up some loose knots here and there. (Note: I don't know that much of Exalted lore, so shoot me if the analogy is weird)<br /> <br /> By the way, are &quot;Fatewalkers&quot; an official name for liberated Deceived?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:29:12-08:00","id":1023099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1023097#post1023097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Well, I'm still stealing it if I ever have to come up with a name for them. (I was pondering &quot;Liberated&quot; myself)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:33:50-08:00","id":1023101,"title":"","content":"I don't think Fate is enough of anything other than an inscrutable cosmic force to make servants for itself. Near as I can tell, the Rite of Return was stapling something onto its tide rather than any sort of pact with that, and that free of the influences of the Judges and Shan'iatu, it's what remains for an Arisen to be anchored to rather than the new boss that has selected them. Fate seems content to work through coincidences, and less the &quot;what are the odds that I have the one Relic that can kill this thing?&quot; sort of coincidences over &quot;what if one Arisen woke up four years before the Sothic Turn should've woken them up and we see what happens?&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:15:57-08:00","id":1023186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1023083#post1023083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*As conceived of in the Curse sense, as opposed to Lost or Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, 3 Fates walk into a bar... wait a minute.<br /> <br /> I wonder which Fate each gameline would correspond to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:27:22-08:00","id":1024500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1022607#post1022607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maintain that the Rite of Return was a singular occult act that required the ritual sacrifice of <i>an entire empire</i> to fuel it at the direct behest of some godlike supernatural entities whose origins we don't truly understand, and that duplicating that is both silly and undermines the fundamental loneliness and temporal distance that the Arisen experience that provides some of the thematic core of the game.<br /> <br /> But I'm no fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm no fun back the other way. Cause I continue to believe that one can take all of these things into account and still introduce various variations on the Arisen from one ancient culture or another without doing harm to any of the established backstory or themes. The trick is numbers and intensity. One doesn't NEED to introduce another magic empire to be swallowed up in some fantastic rite that produces hundreds to thousands (we don't have a firm number of Arisen, so the precise scale created in the Rite is open to interpretation) of resurrected corpses. The canon already has vessels produced in other ancient eras by individuals with no apparent connection to Irem. The canon can support individual sorcerers who discover a trickle more about the nature of Sekhem, enough to replicate something akin to the Rite on a smaller scale with aspects unique to the culture and region. Something that produces at most dozens of entities rather than hundreds. Enough to watch over a forgotten city or serve a single dynasty of kings. Rare enough to keep an Arisen's existence lonely and not be a true rival to old Irem. Unique enough to inject more variety into the beings the Arisen encounter, threaten, and befriend. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:43:38-08:00","id":1024553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1024500#post1024500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm no fun back the other way. Cause I continue to believe that one can take all of these things into account and still introduce various variations on the Arisen from one ancient culture or another without doing harm to any of the established backstory or themes. The trick is numbers and intensity. One doesn't NEED to introduce another magic empire to be swallowed up in some fantastic rite that produces hundreds to thousands (we don't have a firm number of Arisen, so the precise scale created in the Rite is open to interpretation) of resurrected corpses. The canon already has vessels produced in other ancient eras by individuals with no apparent connection to Irem. The canon can support individual sorcerers who discover a trickle more about the nature of Sekhem, enough to replicate something akin to the Rite on a smaller scale with aspects unique to the culture and region. Something that produces at most dozens of entities rather than hundreds. Enough to watch over a forgotten city or serve a single dynasty of kings. Rare enough to keep an Arisen's existence lonely and not be a true rival to old Irem. Unique enough to inject more variety into the beings the Arisen encounter, threaten, and befriend.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, as has been discussed to no resolution multiple times, how much do these beings mirror the Arisen's mechanics and powers? Why would they? And if they don't, why are we even calling them the same class of being?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:53:09-08:00","id":1024774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1024553#post1024553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, as has been discussed to no resolution multiple times, how much do these beings mirror the Arisen's mechanics and powers? Why would they? And if they don't, why are we even calling them the same class of being?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sekhem is a universal force in the Mummy mythos,so effective means to infuse things or beings with Sekhem and the results of so doing, are going to have commonalities. And those with more commonalities will be more likely to ping a Deathless and their cult's list of things to look out for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:22:59-08:00","id":1024960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1024774#post1024774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sekhem is a universal force in the Mummy mythos,so effective means to infuse things or beings with Sekhem and the results of so doing, are going to have commonalities. And those with more commonalities will be more likely to ping a Deathless and their cult's list of things to look out for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, things to look for. But the big question that this thread is about is non-Iremite mummies. Other cultures can (and have) harnessed Sekhem... but just using Sekhem is a long way from being able to whip up true immortals like the Arisen (and Deceived).<br /> <br /> So, say you have culture X that has figured out how to harness Sekhem. Without the tutelage of crazy god-monsters. Say they even use it to preserve some champions in an undying state. Are these beings really Mummies? When so much of the underlying metaphysical structure is bound to be different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:23:43-08:00","id":1024961,"title":"","content":"So it appears that the two base arguments being made (and please correct me if I've missed any) are 1. Inscrutable as it is, Fate is not a decision-maker, but rather an impersonal force; and 2. The creation of the Arisen required an entire civilization's worth of life and effort, how could any other Deathless exist with less effort, much less by accident?<br /> <br /> To answer these issues, let us consider the potential for non-Iremite Arisen in terms of cause and effect. The creation of the Arisen was a massive effect, a veritable supernatural atom bomb. Now, the cause has been well established (the sacrifice of Irem), and on the face of it, so has the effect (the Arisen). But, suppose the effect wasn't simply the Arisen themselves, but the very possibility that being such as the Deathless could exist in the first place (as my original hypothesis posited). To that end, and following the atom bomb analogy, if the direct consequences of the explosion are the creation of the Arisen (by the Shan'iatu's design) and Shuankhsen (by Ammut's machinations), then the drifting fallout on the wind would be the aforementioned unique Deathless.<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:30:08-08:00","id":1024962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1024961#post1024961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it appears that the two base arguments being made (and please correct me if I've missed any) are 1. Inscrutable as it is, Fate is not a decision-maker, but rather an impersonal force; and 2. The creation of the Arisen required an entire civilization's worth of life and effort, how could any other Deathless exist with less effort, much less by accident?<br /> <br /> To answer these issues, let us consider the potential for non-Iremite Arisen in terms of cause and effect. The creation of the Arisen was a massive effect, a veritable supernatural atom bomb. Now, the cause has been well established (the sacrifice of Irem), and on the face of it, so has the effect (the Arisen). But, suppose the effect wasn't simply the Arisen themselves, but the very possibility that being such as the Deathless could exist in the first place (as my original hypothesis posited). To that end, and following the atom bomb analogy, if the direct consequences of the explosion are the creation of the Arisen (by the Shan'iatu's design) and Shuankhsen (by Ammut's machinations), then the drifting fallout on the wind would be the aforementioned unique Deathless.<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A valid supposition (considering what we know about the details of the Rite of Return).<br /> <br /> Though the question remains how close would these hypothetical non-Irem Arisen be to Irem Arisen mechanically. Pillars? Unlikely (too rooted in Iremite theology and metaphysics). Utterances? Fine... except there would need to be an alternate way to power them (see Pillars). Judges? Unlikely, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T19:22:04-08:00","id":1024978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1024962#post1024962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A valid supposition (considering what we know about the details of the Rite of Return).<br /> <br /> Though the question remains how close would these hypothetical non-Irem Arisen be to Irem Arisen mechanically. Pillars? Unlikely (too rooted in Iremite theology and metaphysics). Utterances? Fine... except there would need to be an alternate way to power them (see Pillars). Judges? Unlikely, I'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that, as a product of some of the most intensive examinations of the soul currently revealed in the CoD, the Pillars would be the same in function, if not necessarily in form. To whit, these foreign Deathless would not know of the Pillars as such, but could still cultivate and use them, even if only on an unconscious level. For instance, a Deathless from a South American culture wouldn't know about Sheut, but would recognize that a particular ability feels rooted in a dark, base part of their being.<br /> <br /> Utterances? Yes, they would largely stay the same, though some imagery may change to match the Deathless' given theology and environment.<br /> <br /> As for Judges...well, I suppose that some beings, if they exist and are aware of these Deathless, may act in similar roles and functions. I'll need to think on how such beings would affect powers or Memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 12-31-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T04:28:33-08:00","id":1025049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1024962#post1024962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though the question remains how close would these hypothetical non-Irem Arisen be to Irem Arisen mechanically. Pillars? Unlikely (too rooted in Iremite theology and metaphysics). Utterances? Fine... except there would need to be an alternate way to power them (see Pillars). Judges? Unlikely, I'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view. Pillars: depends whether you consider the fivefold soul to be something Irem invented or something Irem discovered. The latter would mean it's always true - though I would have it that any non-Iremites who manage to create mummies only manage to create ones with a single functional Pillar (which they would likely identity with whatever their metaphysics designates as the seat of spiritual power). Affinities and Utterances: potentially yes, but the above would limit which were available (though they might also have their own unique ones). Judges: no, and probably no equivalent. Descent: yes, in some form (I don't think the Descent is optimal for the purposes the Arisen were designed for, which means the Shan'iatu were bound by a design constraint there, which means anyone else who manages to make a Sekhem-infused being will be bound by it to). Mummified: usually, yes (the kind of magic we're dealing with here draws little distinction between visceral and spiritual, and requiring the preservation of the body as a means to align with pure Sekhem is a good way to represent that; having said that, there might be other options, of lesser power) (also, non-animated mummified bodies make pretty good uter). Sybaris: yes (that's the weight of Sekhem talking IMO). Vessels: I would allow other categories. Kepher: maybe, but it would be aligned to the purpose for which the Sekhem-infused being was made (a mummified ancestor raised as a protector for a community might sense dangers to it; someone pursuing their own enlightenment might sense potential lessons to learn).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T06:40:30-08:00","id":1025064,"title":"","content":"While I don't mind the idea of other cultures practicing mummification in mimicry of the Deathless, creating botched or lesser varieties, the whole genre of 'mummy horror' is totally Egyptian (as in Hollywood).<br /> <br /> If there were to be something else that are sort of parallel to the Deathless but from another culture I think it should be as grounded in that culture's mythology as much as the Deathless are to ancient Egyptian. To me at least, <b>Mummy</b> is a game steeped in its divine beings and otherworldly gods. There are many beings in the <b>CofD</b> that are god-like but Azar, Sotek, and Anpu are really a different class, or should be treated as such.<br /> <br /> So I feel like a 'foreign peer' of the Deathless would not necessarily be mummies, but they may be jaded divine servants their own","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T05:50:08-08:00","id":1025387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1025064#post1025064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I feel like a 'foreign peer' of the Deathless would not necessarily be mummies, but they may be jaded divine servants their own</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend where I'm using them. If it's by themselves, then I would do what you suggest. If it's all over the WoD, then I would create a generic &quot;Ancestor&quot; type supernatural, some variants of which would be mummified undead. If it's in a strictly Mummy the Curse game, then Sekhem would work how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T22:50:59-08:00","id":1028046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1025064#post1025064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't mind the idea of other cultures practicing mummification in mimicry of the Deathless, creating botched or lesser varieties, the whole genre of 'mummy horror' is totally Egyptian (as in Hollywood).</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that I'll be replying to other chunks of your post in quotation marks because this site vexes me and I am too tired to figure out what is up with it.<br /> <br /> I agree, especially with the first part. In fact, I would suggest that any entity encountered by the Deathless should fall into that conveniently wide range of nasties they call the Lifeless. That being said, I would argue that the &quot;mummy horror&quot; genre is far more Hollywood than Egyptian. Yeah, the Nile had some legends of the dead coming back, but what we think of as mummy horror is due far more to modern storytelling. Why do I harp on this? Because I think this essentially provides all the elements you need to tell an authentic &quot;mummy horror&quot; story while still stripping it of the Egyptian setting. Not that the culture is unimportant- in most mummy movies its vital to unearth lost history in order to defeat the monster. But thematically I think the bare bones Hollywood has established is what can unite a Mummy story from a different culture. Impossibly ancient, bearing secrets long forgotten but are horrifically dangerous when used against the modern age, merciless to those that violate its rest or obstruct its purpose, that kind of thing. <br /> <br /> &quot;If there were to be something else that are sort of parallel to the Deathless but from another culture I think it should be as grounded in that culture's mythology as much as the Deathless are to ancient Egyptian. To me at least, <b>Mummy</b> is a game steeped in its divine beings and otherworldly gods. There are many beings in the <b>CofD</b> that are god-like but Azar, Sotek, and Anpu are really a different class, or should be treated as such.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think there are some things to keep and some things to toss. Memory- keep it. Its thematically appropriate for a several thousand year old entity. Descent. Keep it. Also thematically appropriate to have a time limit that the entity can walk among the living. Sybaris? Yeah, although maybe change the name. I would base Pillars off of local custom and understanding of the soul, and possibly shift the number of pillars around as appropriate. Say, for instance, a Chinese Daoist would have access to two pillars because their understanding of the soul is based on Yin and Yang. Meanwhile, a Greek alchemist might divide their pillars into four categories based on the classic elements. Gods....keep it ambiguous I say. When these things die do they go to Duat...or are there other realms beyond the veil of death unknown even to the Judges? Play with it. Same with Attainments and such. Give them abilities unique to the Mummy and the culture it comes from.<br /> <br /> &quot;So I feel like a 'foreign peer' of the Deathless would not necessarily be mummies, but they may be jaded divine servants their own&quot;<br /> <br /> I get what you are saying, but we already have several options from other rules sets if we want the Deathless to face down something totally new. My first preference would be to work within the rules system and change the portions steeped in the Egyptian into something else rather than jump outside the gameline proper. Although if second edition wanted to include more things that last forever that aren't Deathless or Lifeless, that'd be cool. Living immortals and reincarnations spring immediately to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T23:34:26-08:00","id":1028056,"title":"","content":"Actually I wasn't saying the Foreign Divine Servants should be made with rules outside of <b>Mummy </b>gameline. I'm saying it'd be more thematically appropriate to have 'non-Iremite divine entities' than 'non-Iremite mummies.'<br /> <br /> I'd love for there to be something unique and scary in a Night Horrors supplement for the game, but otherwise there's Osiran Prometheans, Hollow Mekhet vampires, strange versions of the Bound, and the entirety of the Immortals supplement. I love the implications that another culture's mockery of the Rite just feeds more to the Devourer, too, and just creates more Shuankhsen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T13:03:33-08:00","id":1028245,"title":"","content":"while I'm not sure about other cultures creating Deathless (or even Lifeless) creatures, I'm totally in favor of other cultures making, well something. I mean, Sekhem is meant to be a universal force of reality, doesn't it? Other cultures should have learned how to shape it, creating relics, terrible monsters, Amkhata like beings, mutated breeds, crazy constructs, traditions of Sekhem sorcerers, mad ghosts and perhaps some few true immortals. Something which reflects the culture which made them, yet is powered by the same cosmic forces which power the Arisen. Something which would give a new perspective to the Arisen cosmology, creating new mysteries and showing that the world is wider than Irem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T15:40:26-08:00","id":1028296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1028245#post1028245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while I'm not sure about other cultures creating Deathless (or even Lifeless) creatures, I'm totally in favor of other cultures making, well something. I mean, Sekhem is meant to be a universal force of reality, doesn't it? Other cultures should have learned how to shape it, creating relics, terrible monsters, Amkhata like beings, mutated breeds, crazy constructs, traditions of Sekhem sorcerers, mad ghosts and perhaps some few true immortals. Something which reflects the culture which made them, yet is powered by the same cosmic forces which power the Arisen. Something which would give a new perspective to the Arisen cosmology, creating new mysteries and showing that the world is wider than Irem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, every culture has the ability to make relics. That's the Sekhem manipulation accessible to every culture.<br /> <br /> Amkhata also fit in to a lot of different cultures. They're feathered serpents, chimera, all kinds of different demigods and demons. Hybrid monsters aren't uncommon in a lot of mythology.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't feel any culture should be able to create something of a nature with Arisen or Shuankhsen. Irem was exceptional, unique. The Arisen weren't the product of human sorcerers, but of the children of the Judges themselves working in concert with an all-devouring maw and the sacrifice of their entire civilisation. That isn't something I feel comfortable being replicated by a regular human culture. <br /> <br /> But let's all bear in mind that the Mummy core book actually does provide rules on how to make non-Iremite Mummies and undead. Intruders and Revenants can have the aesthetics of a non-Iremite Mummy and still be well within the means for any culture to create. Their rules can be used to recreate all kinds of different undead horrors, and they've been my go-to whenever I want to create the appearance of some culture attempting to mimic the glory of Irem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T04:46:34-08:00","id":1028500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1028245#post1028245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while I'm not sure about other cultures creating Deathless (or <b>even Lifeless</b>) creatures, I'm totally in favor of other cultures making...terrible monsters, Amkhata like beings, mutated breeds, crazy constructs...mad ghosts and perhaps some few true immortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the monsters you mention could arguably be lumped under the rather broad umbrella of Lifeless. A few powers in the core even refer to vampires as such.<br /> <br /> Your post is a good point, though, when you mention that Sekhem is a universal force so surely others must have noticed it over the ages. Still, it took <i>gods</i> sacrificing an empire while bargaining with the embodiment of entropy to create the Rite of Return. I think other civilizations <i>at best </i>would end up with lesser immortals, ghosts, or straight up Shuankhsen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:43:42-08:00","id":1028606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1028500#post1028500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it took <i>gods</i> sacrificing an empire while bargaining with the embodiment of entropy to create the Rite of Return. I think other civilizations <i>at best </i>would end up with lesser immortals, ghosts, or straight up Shuankhsen</div> </div> </div> </div>with this I agree- no other culture should make something which is truly like the Arisen. I have little interest in &quot;made in China Irem&quot; (I mean it literally in that context). The Rite of Return was a unique event, and other cultures should have their own, unique events (perhaps not as dramatic as the Nameless Empire, but things which express those cultures instead of just copying from Irem). If they did made immortals of their own, they should either be singular creations or operate under some very different system. It should take work to make those, sure, but other cultures deserve more than &quot;just like the Arisen, only with another name&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:24:10-08:00","id":1028648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1028606#post1028606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> with this I agree- no other culture should make something which is truly like the Arisen. I have little interest in &quot;made in China Irem&quot; (I mean it literally in that context). The Rite of Return was a unique event, and other cultures should have their own, unique events (perhaps not as dramatic as the Nameless Empire, but things which express those cultures instead of just copying from Irem). If they did made immortals of their own, they should either be singular creations or operate under some very different system. It should take work to make those, sure, but other cultures deserve more than &quot;just like the Arisen, only with another name&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely.<br /> <br /> ...which is why I'm always confused as to why these discussions happen in the Mummy forum rather than the general forum. Immortals are a blue book minor splat, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T20:27:53-08:00","id":1028849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1028500#post1028500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it took <i>gods</i> sacrificing an empire while bargaining with the embodiment of entropy to create the Rite of Return. I think other civilizations <i>at best </i>would end up with lesser immortals, ghosts, or straight up Shuankhsen</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on this, but do remember that it isn't the civilization that is creating these new Arisen. Rather, whatever ritual trappings they use are acting as a lightning rod for the storm that the Shan'iatu called up ages ago. The culture only provides a social and theological (and maybe supernatural) framework for the new mummy to base their existence on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:08:50-08:00","id":1028858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1028849#post1028849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you on this, but do remember that it isn't the civilization that is creating these new Arisen. Rather, whatever ritual trappings they use are acting as a lightning rod for the storm that the Shan'iatu called up ages ago. The culture only provides a social and theological (and maybe supernatural) framework for the new mummy to base their existence on.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few references in the Book of the Deceived actually made me think the Rite of Return took things in the opposite direction. Magic was drained out of the world by the Rite. The world described by the Shan'iatu before the founding of Irem is one in which a lot more magic seems to be roiling around than made it to the present day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T05:26:27-08:00","id":1029561,"title":"","content":"While there does seem like there might be less magic, what makes you think it was the Rite itself that drained it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T00:17:18-08:00","id":1029951,"title":"","content":"Query: would the Purified (from <b>World of Darkness: Immortals</b>) count as Deathless or Lifeless? Because they're what I'd use as a baseline for non-Iremite mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:15:40-08:00","id":1029959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1029561#post1029561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there does seem like there might be less magic, what makes you think it was the Rite itself that drained it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this memory of some throw-away line in one of the Mummy books (like I said, I think it might have been Book of the Deceived) that gave me that impression. There's a chance it was just talking about the hiding of Seba from the world, but I thought it was actually about something a bit more concrete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1029951#post1029951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: would the Purified (from <b>World of Darkness: Immortals</b>) count as Deathless or Lifeless? Because they're what I'd use as a baseline for non-Iremite mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not undead at all, right? Wouldn't count as either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:06:08-08:00","id":1029993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1029951#post1029951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: would the Purified (from <b>World of Darkness: Immortals</b>) count as Deathless or Lifeless? Because they're what I'd use as a baseline for non-Iremite mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Arisen would definitely count them among the Lifeless. Whether they ought to is a different question (though at least one meaning of &quot;Lifeless&quot; seems to be &quot;undead or immortal being we don't understand enough to bother respecting,&quot; which applies to the Purified well enough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 01-11-2017, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T05:17:08-08:00","id":1030010,"title":"","content":"I like the points you're making in response to mine, and I agree with them all.<br /> <br /> The books basically state that the Deathless are 'true' mummies, one defining feature at least being the Memory trait, and every other undead thing as Lifeless...though amkhata are counted among Lifeless so idk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:02:32-08:00","id":1030035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies?p=1029951#post1029951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: would the Purified (from <b>World of Darkness: Immortals</b>) count as Deathless or Lifeless? Because they're what I'd use as a baseline for non-Iremite mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they would count as either. Purified are more like human-Spirits (or Spirits that think they are the original person...?), in that they interact with Spirits, use Essence like Spirits, can reform like Spirits, etc. I could easily see a Ghost variant that might get classified as Lifeless, but one distinguishing thing about the Purified is that they are alive when they are in their body (not using a life-like mask, as the Arisen do, nor &quot;faking&quot; life signs, like vampires do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}